      "created_at": "2017-09-14T19:00:05Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-09-14T19:00:05Z",
      "body": "Because of open source nature of project it is impossible to create spoof resistant procedure of telemetry collecting. Any checksum calculation or ciphering are not useful because of open source.  So I think it can be as simple as sending single plain text UDP packet without any acknowledgement and/or session establishment. Also collecting machine name or mac addresses are too intrusive IMHO. May be every installation should generate installation UUID  and send them. Not sure, does we really need any kind of ID to distinguish reports those had come from different installations, if we intent only to statistic collection. ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
