      "created_at": "2017-09-14T21:14:26Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-09-14T21:14:26Z",
      "body": "> Also collecting machine name or mac addresses are too intrusive IMHO.\r\n\r\nOf course. I simply meant combining them, using them to \"sign\" each signature. Some features, like how many times the RSS downloader is used for example - would not need the signed collection. It would be only used if you wanted to see if people ever turned an option on, like ever. Or something like that. Probably it is indeed an overkill.\r\n\r\nOff the bat, simple packages would do indeed, but the server side still has to be written by someone. In Java maybe? I don't know. Or maybe there is an open-source library/solution for this?",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
