      "created_at": "2017-09-15T02:59:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-09-15T02:59:46Z",
      "body": "Before going to code we should elaborate a clear protocol description. And before the protocol creation we should determine what kind of an information would be collected. For me, there are two different types of information:\r\n1. Answering to \"_What is ?_\". Examples: \"_what is OS version?_\", \"_what is some option's checkbox position?_\".\r\n2. Answering to \"_How many times ... per period?_\". Example: \"_how many times torrent added last month._\"\r\n\r\nFirst type obviously will be collected. But second type looks like considerable more difficult to collect, so we should at first decide, will we collect this type at all.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
