      "created_at": "2017-10-08T12:57:37Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-10-08T13:00:35Z",
      "body": "Sorry. I meant the things _used_ in the client, like how many times you use a search provider. The numbers would simply say \"10 people used X provider in the past 30 days\". Or something like that. There is still nothing baked here, it's in \"idea-phase.\"\r\n\r\nDev wise... there are no core devs on the project that are paid to work on the client's whatever aspect. This was just an idea out of the blue, thrown in. Anyone can pick it up (dzmat is already looking around), and I am willing to support the idea (just like any other qBittorrent related idea) with the server resources.\r\n\r\nBy the way, in my opinion, this could be used to reduce dev load. Because devs keep adding new features that users ask for. And there is nothing wrong with that - but having more features mean more features you have to keep updated. It just equals more work. So it would be good to see if various features are used at all. If there is something that no one uses, we could further discuss if it's viable to keep it around. Or what part needs more development work, what's the most used feature. \r\n\r\nAgain, that is also just an idea. Having just the numbers is already \"fun\". :)",
      "author_association": "NONE",
