      "created_at": "2019-04-23T11:27:19Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-04-23T11:27:19Z",
      "body": "> All the stats would be anonymous of course\r\n\r\nI see this was opened pre-GDPR, so consider this:\r\n\r\nThere is no such thing as anonymous when you are receiving the IP address of the sender. Considering that according to GDPR the IP address is personal data and any processing of personal data must be based on:\r\n\r\n- informed choice\r\n- freely given (not forced) consent\r\n\r\nany such option should:\r\n\r\n1. Be OFF by default (= it should be an **opt-in**, not an opt out)\r\n2. Inform the user of the consequences of its enabling (for him, not for the data controller)\r\n3. Give him an option to still be able to use the program without opting in.\r\n\r\n> Don't shoot please.\r\n\r\nToo late. You have been shot :P\r\n\r\nIf one chooses FOSS one chooses its for the freedom it gives. Usually telemetry and stats are aimed to optimize a product/service commercially, i.e. it benefits a centralized entity.",
